From e265e2bd6faa77cbc70b461b49458a6ae33be996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:04:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix authorization bug and add full CRUD API for all domain
 entities

Fixes:
- require_project_access: the write-restriction check for CLIENT_PM/
  CLIENT_USER never triggered (it tested a role condition that was
  already guaranteed false). Now CLIENT_USER is read-only and CLIENT_PM
  can write within its own client scope.
- project_financials: timesheet status filter compared against a string
  literal instead of the TimesheetStatus enum.
- Task.wbs_code now unique per project (uq_task_project_wbs).
- Task.actual_hours is recalculated from approved timesheets whenever a
  timesheet is approved/rejected (was previously always zero).
- Added the scripts/configurar_porta_3035.sh referenced by the README
  but missing from the repository.

New endpoints (previously missing per-entity CRUD):
- Clients, Users (bootstrap admin + demonstrative login), Projects,
  Project intakes, Tasks/EAP (+ reschedule endpoint), task dependencies,
  task assignments, Resources, Timesheets (list/approve/reject),
  Project expenses, Calendars/Holidays, Risks, Change requests,
  Baselines.

Restructured app/main.py into app/db.py, app/deps.py, app/schemas.py,
app/security.py and one router per resource under app/routers/.

Added tests: authorization regression tests, service-layer regression
tests for the two fixed bugs, and API-level integration tests covering
the bootstrap/login/project/task/timesheet-approval flow and the
CLIENT_USER write-block behavior.

Note: this environment could not reach PyPI to install dependencies and
run pytest (network egress restricted); all files pass python3 -m
py_compile and were reviewed manually. Run `pip install -r
requirements.txt && PYTHONPATH=. pytest -q` to execute the suite.
